[center][size=6][b][color=#4fc3f7]7   D A S H E S   T O   D I E[/color][/b][/size]
[size=4][i]Rule 1 was cardio. Rule 2 is not standing still.[/i][/size]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/HannaPanda/7D2D-7DashesToDie/refs/heads/main/nexus/images/DashHero.jpg[/img][/center]

A horde rounds the corner. Normally that is the moment you find out how far the nearest doorway is. With this mod it is the moment you tap a key and are somewhere else.

[b]7 Dashes to Die[/b] adds a [b]dash[/b], an [b]air dash[/b] and a [b]double air dash[/b], earned rather than given. They live behind a new Agility perk that sits right next to Parkour: [b]Rule 2: Double Tap[/b].

[center][color=#4fc3f7]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#4fc3f7]Balance feedback[/color][/b][/size]
The feature set is complete, but dash force and balance may still change. If you adjust the [b]Force[/b] slider, leave the percentage you settled on in the [b]Posts[/b] tab.

[center][color=#4fc3f7]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#4fc3f7]Features[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Dash[/b] - a burst of speed in the direction you are moving. No input means straight ahead.
[*][b]Air dash[/b] - cancels your fall, so it carries you [i]flat[/i] across a gap instead of down into it.
[*][b]Double air dash[/b] - two dashes per jump at the last rank, recharging the moment you land.
[*]Costs stamina and has a cooldown.
[*][b]Localized into 13 languages[/b]: EN, DE, ES, FR, IT, JA, KO, PL, PT-BR, RU, TR, ZH-Hans, ZH-Hant.
[/list]

[size=5][b][color=#4fc3f7]Perk ranks[/color][/b][/size]
[b]Rule 2: Double Tap[/b] sits under [i]Agility ▸ Athletics[/i], with the same requirements as every vanilla Agility perk.

[list=1]
[*][b]Rank 1[/b] (Agility 1) - unlocks the ground dash.
[*][b]Rank 2[/b] (Agility 3) - stronger dash, shorter cooldown.
[*][b]Rank 3[/b] (Agility 5) - [b]unlocks the air dash[/b].
[*][b]Rank 4[/b] (Agility 7) - stronger dash, shorter cooldown.
[*][b]Rank 5[/b] (Agility 10) - [b]unlocks the double air dash[/b].
[/list]

[size=5][b][color=#4fc3f7]Keybinding and controller[/color][/b][/size]
Rebind the dash under [i]Options ▸ Controls ▸ Movement[/i], in the [i]Player movement[/i] group. Default is [b]V[/b].

[b]On a controller[/b] it has its own row under [i]Options ▸ Controller ▸ On Foot[/i], rebindable like any vanilla one. It ships [b]unbound[/b], since vanilla already uses just about every button. Put it on whatever you have spare.

[size=5][b][color=#4fc3f7]Double tap to dash[/color][/b][/size]
You can also [b]tap a movement key twice and dash that way[/b]. Double-tap A and you dodge left, even if you are holding W at the time. The dash key keeps working as before.

It is [b]off by default[/b], since a mis-read tap costs stamina and moves you somewhere you did not ask to go. Turn it on in the settings and tune the window: the default is [b]300 ms[/b], lower it toward 150 if dashes fire on their own while you strafe, raise it toward 600 if you keep trying and nothing happens.

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/HannaPanda/7D2D-7DashesToDie/refs/heads/main/nexus/images/DashKey.jpg[/img][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#4fc3f7]Settings[/color][/b][/size]
[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/7daystodie/mods/4017][b]Gears[/b][/url] is optional. With it you get a settings page under [i]Mods ▸ 7 Dashes to Die[/i], reachable from the main menu or the ESC menu; without it the mod runs on its defaults.
[list]
[*][b]Enabled[/b] - on or off.
[*][b]Require perk[/b] - turn it off to use the dash without spending skill points.
[*][b]Force[/b] - 25 to 300%. Controls how strongly the dash launches you; roughly 10 m at the default.
[*][b]Cooldown[/b] - 0.2 to 10 seconds. Higher perk ranks shorten it further.
[*][b]Stamina cost[/b] - 0 to 50. Set it to 0 for a free dash.
[*][b]Volume[/b] - 0 to 100%, on top of your normal game volume.
[*][b]Double tap to dash[/b] - enables directional dashing by double-tapping a movement key.
[*][b]Double tap window[/b] - controls how quickly the second tap must follow.
[/list]
Setting changes apply immediately. [b]No restart, no new save.[/b]

[quote]Settings you have changed yourself are [b]kept[/b] across updates. If you never touched a slider, an update can move it.[/quote]

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/HannaPanda/7D2D-7DashesToDie/refs/heads/main/nexus/images/DashOptions.jpg[/img][/center]

[center][color=#4fc3f7]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#4fc3f7]Known Limitations[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]There is no dash animation.[/b] In first person you will not notice; other players see you glide.
[*][b]On a laggy connection your dash looks snappier to you than to everyone else.[/b]
[/list]

[size=5][b][color=#4fc3f7]Requirements and Installation[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Tested on V 3.0.0, V 3.0.1 and V 3.1.0.[/b] Other 3.x versions have not been tested.
[*][b]EasyAntiCheat must be disabled.[/b] Single-player and private servers.
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/7daystodie/mods/4017][b]Gears[/b][/url] is [b]optional[/b], only for the settings menu. Gears itself needs Quartz.
[*][b]Multiplayer:[/b] install on both client and server.
[/list]
Install the zip with Vortex or MO2, or extract the [i]SevenDashesToDie[/i] folder into [i]7 Days To Die/Mods/[/i], launch with EAC off, then spend a point on [i]Agility ▸ Athletics ▸ Rule 2: Double Tap[/i].

Adding and removing mid-save are both safe. Removing it takes the perk out of the skill tree, and the points you spent on it go with it. Nothing else is touched.

[center][color=#4fc3f7]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

